{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 27, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, who is known for his quick-witted dialogue and engaging storylines. the film stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, the co-founder and CEO of facebook, and andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, zuckerberg's friend and business partner.\n\nthe movie begins with mark zuckerberg, a sophomore at harvard university, who is trying to get into one of the school's exclusive final clubs. after being rejected, zuckerberg creates a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes popular, but also gets zuckerberg into trouble with the school administration.\n\nlater, zuckerberg is approached by twin brothers cameron and tyler winklevoss, who want him to help them create a social networking site for harvard students. zuckerberg agrees, but eventually drops out of the project and creates his own site, which he calls \"thefacebook\". the site quickly gains popularity, and zuckerberg becomes a celebrity on campus.\n\nhowever, zuckerberg's success is short-lived, as he soon finds himself in a series of lawsuits with the winklevoss brothers, who claim that he stole their idea, and with saverin, who claims that zuckerberg cheated him out of his share of the company. the movie follows these lawsuits, as well as zuckerberg's personal struggles, including his relationship with his girlfriend erica albright, played by rooney mara.\n\none of the strengths of the movie is its dialogue, which is quick-witted and engaging. the film's script is full of clever one-liners and humorous moments, which add to the movie's entertainment value. the film's cast is also excellent, with eisenberg and garfield delivering standout performances.\n\nthe movie's themes of ambition, greed, and the consequences of success are also well-explored. the film shows how zuckerberg's desire for success and recognition leads him to make decisions that ultimately hurt the people around him, including his friends and family. the movie also explores the idea that success is not always what it seems, and that the pursuit of wealth and power can come at a great personal cost.\n\noverall, the social network is a well-made and engaging film that tells a fascinating story. the movie's dialogue, cast, and themes all come together to create a compelling and thought-provoking film that is sure to appeal to a wide range of audiences.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.0028338772244751453}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0297507643699646}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.004086359404027462}, {"token": " a", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.20617452263832092}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.00014220656885299832}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.4515504240989685}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.002854917198419571}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.012603159993886948}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00012194366718176752}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.12692804634571075}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.3834453821182251}, {"token": " lawsuits", "logprob": -0.6431171298027039}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -2.4318398573086597e-05}, {"token": " followed", "logprob": -0.00037424711626954377}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -5.602820692729438e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0006680640508420765}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -3.099436753473128e-06}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.